SUMMARY:Felipe Esparza "Laughter Will Save Us" Tour
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, 123 S Walnut Street\, Bloomington
DESCRIPTION:Felipe Esparza is a Mexican-American comedian\, actor\, and pod
 caster known for his irreverent\, working class\,\n“everyman” style of 
 stand-up comedy\, his laid-back attitude and his familiar phrase\, “what
 ’s up fool?”. Despite his\nself-proclaimed laziness\, over the last 30 
 years\, Felipe has been very busy\, managing to put together 5 stand-up\nco
 medy specials for Netflix and HBO (including one in Spanish)\, hosting 3 di
 fferent\, popular\, weekly podcasts – one\nof which has been around for 1
 2 years so far\, winning NBC’s Last Comic Standing back in 2010 and havin
 g recurring\nroles on series such as “The Eric Andre Show”\, “Superst
 ore”\, and “Victor and Valentino”. He’s also had a few\nappearances
  in films including “Blue Beetle” with Xolo Mariduena and George Lopez\
 , “You People” with Eddie\nMurphy and Jonah Hill\, “Guest House” wi
 th Pauly Shore and “7th & Union” with Omar Chaparro.\nFelipe is embarki
 ng on his new "Laughter Will Save Us" tour which hits clubs and theaters ac
 ross the U.S. beginning\nfall 2026.\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/com
 edy-atlas/event/felipe-esparza-laughter-will-save-us-tour/
